{"content":[{"c":["MEDEBA"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Moabite town in the fertile plain northeast of the Dead Sea, about 25 miles (40.2 kilometers) south of Philadelphia (modern Amman). It was situated 6 miles (9.7 kilometers) south of Heshbon on the Roman road to Kerak."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Here the Amorites defeated Moab (",{"href":"?bref=Num.21.30","r":"Num.21.30","rawR":"Num.21.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.21.30","value":"Num.21.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 21:30"},"). Later, Israel defeated Sihon, king of the Amorites, at Medeba and assigned it to Reuben’s tribe (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.13.9,16","r":"Josh.13.9,16","rawR":"Josh.13.9,16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.13.9,16","value":"Josh.13.9,16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 13:9, 16"},"). At this place David routed an Aramean army hired by the Ammonites to attack his forces (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.19.7","r":"1Chr.19.7","rawR":"1Chr.19.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.19.7","value":"1Chr.19.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 19:7"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["According to the Moabite Stone, the town was once controlled by Omri and Ahab of Israel; however, when Mesha reasserted Moabite dominance in the eighth century ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},", he rebuilt Medeba and other Moabite cities. Medeba is named in Isaiah’s prophecies against Moab (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.15.2","r":"Isa.15.2","rawR":"Isa.15.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.15.2","value":"Isa.15.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 15:2"},"). In later times Joram and Jehoshaphat made unsuccessful attempts at capturing this city."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Medeba","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 21:30","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.21.30","rawQueryValue":"Num.21.30","sourceRefExact":"Num.21.30"},{"anchorText":"Jos 13:9, 16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.13.9,16","rawQueryValue":"Josh.13.9,16","sourceRefExact":"Josh.13.9,16"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 19:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.19.7","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.19.7","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.19.7"},{"anchorText":"Is 15:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.15.2","rawQueryValue":"Isa.15.2","sourceRefExact":"Isa.15.2"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"864b512527dd919f6240c4f1c344632a993c80de86e15e6118f9a5124ba2b756","sourceItemName":"Medeba","sourceItemOrder":201,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Medeba","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Medeba","title":"Medeba","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}